  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Silence the Silent Killer &apos;High Blood Pressure&apos;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to Kenya&apos;s Ministry of Health, nearly one in every four Kenyans aged 20 to 50, and one in every two Kenyans over 50, has hypertension. Sadly, more than half of Kenyans have never had their blood pressure checked. Tharaka Nithi County recorded 27,136 hypertension cases in 2020 and 55,755 outpatient visits in 2021.  Providing BP Machines to CHVs will increase community screening, enhance early diagnosis and treatment and silence the silent killer- Hypertension.</narrative>
  </description>
